# Feedback backend (Firebase) configuration.
#
# The rest of AUREVA needs NO environment variables — this file only
# matters for the new Feedback page. Without these set, the Feedback page
# still renders and explains that the backend isn't configured yet; nothing
# else in the app is affected.
#
# 1. Create a free project at https://console.firebase.google.com
# 2. Add a Web App to it, then copy the config values it gives you below.
# 3. Enable Firestore (Build → Firestore Database → Create database).
# 4. Apply the rules in firestore.rules (Firestore → Rules tab) so writes
#    are anonymous, create-only, and can't be read back publicly.
# 5. Copy this file to ".env" (not committed) and fill in the values.
# 6. Restart `npm run dev` after editing .env.

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# Nearby Care — hospital/clinic search (optional).
#
# Without this set, Nearby Care still fully works: it falls back to a
# Google Maps search link built from the caller's own location (or a
# plain-text search if location wasn't granted) — no key, no cost, no
# missing feature, just a link out instead of in-app result cards.
#
# Setting this key upgrades that to real in-app result cards (name,
# address, phone, directions) via Google's Places API (New).
#
# IMPORTANT — this is a static site with no backend, so any VITE_-
# prefixed variable is bundled into the client and is not truly secret.
# Google's supported pattern for this is an HTTP-referrer-restricted key:
#
# 1. Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Credentials → Create API key
# 2. Enable "Places API (New)" for the project
# 3. Restrict the key: Application restrictions → HTTP referrers →
#    add your deployed domain(s) (e.g. https://yourdomain.com/*)
# 4. Restrict the key: API restrictions → limit to "Places API (New)" only
# 5. Copy the key below
#
# A key without referrer restrictions should never be used here — that's
# what makes this safe to ship in client code rather than a secret leak.
VITE_GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=
